          "why_it_matters": "Passerine has a clear compositional engine rather than a generic small-group premise: Crump is building the music around the different ways birds construct nests, and the quartet gives that idea an unusually open palette—acoustic bass, percussion, trumpet, alto flute and saxophone. With Ches Smith, Kenny Warren and David Leon, the draw is how four strong instrumental voices can turn a concrete natural-world idea into ensemble form and improvisation in Rhizome’s close room.",
